The following are the system resources used by openCryptoki

Please also see https://www.ibm.com/docs/en/linux-on-systems?topic=features-architecture-components-opencryptoki

The user under which pkcsslotd runs (default: pkcsslotd) and the group that all
openCryptoki applications must belong to (default: pkcs11) can be configured at
build time using:
    ./configure --with-pkcsslotd-user=USER --with-pkcs-group=GROUP

Throughout this document PKCSSLOTD_USER refers to that configured user and
PKCS_GROUP refers to that configured group.

Each token can additionally have its own user group, configured per slot in
opencryptoki.conf with the keyword:
    usergroup = GROUP
If usergroup is not set for a slot, TOKEN_GROUP defaults to PKCS_GROUP.
Throughout this document TOKEN_GROUP refers to that per-token group.
All members of TOKEN_GROUP must also be members of PKCS_GROUP.
PKCSSLOTD_USER must also be a member of PKCS_GROUP.

1. Shared memory = 1 per token + 1 segment between pkcsslotd & api + 1 statistic
   segment per user (if statistics are enabled)

    a. Between pkcsslotd and api
       The pkcsslotd daemon has its own shared memory segment that it creates
       and shares with the API library. Part of the data is passed through
       sockets but there is still some data shared via shared memory.
       Owner: PKCSSLOTD_USER  Group: PKCS_GROUP  Mode: 0660 (rw-rw----)
       Size: sizeof(Slot_Mgr_Shr_t) - a fixed structure holding per-process and
       per-slot session counters for up to 1000 processes and 1024 slots.
       Approximately 12 MB on 64-bit platforms.

    b. Each token has its own shared memory segment. openCryptoki processes
       attach to the token segment and shared memory acts as a global state
       tracking mechanism.
       Owner: the first application process to open the token
       Group: TOKEN_GROUP  Mode: 0660 (rw-rw----)
       Size: sizeof(LW_SHM_TYPE) - holds a TOKEN_DATA mirror plus two arrays
       of MAX_TOK_OBJS object index entries (default: 2048 public + 2048
       private). Approximately 65 KB per token at the default setting.
       MAX_TOK_OBJS can be set at build time:
           ./configure --with-max-token-objects=N
       Example segment names visible under /dev/shm:
           var.lib.opencryptoki.ccatok   var.lib.opencryptoki.swtok
           var.lib.opencryptoki.ep11tok  var.lib.opencryptoki.tpm.root
           var.lib.opencryptoki.lite

    c. If collection of statistics is enabled, there is one shared memory
       segment per user. It is created at the first usage of openCryptoki of
       a user, and is named var.lib.opencryptoki_stats_<uid> where <uid> is
       the numeric user id of the user.
       Owner: the user  Group: the user's primary group  Mode: 0600 (rw-------)
       Size: num_configured_slots × MECHTABLE_NUM_ELEMS ×
             (NUM_SUPPORTED_STRENGTHS + 1) × sizeof(CK_ULONG)
           = num_slots × approximately 200 mechanisms × 5 strength buckets
           × 8 bytes = approximately 16 KB per configured slot.
       Use the pkcsstats tool to display the statistics, and remove statistics
       segments for users no longer needed.

2. Sockets - up to 3
   a. Unix socket between pkcsslotd and API processes to transfer slot
      information.
      Path: /run/opencryptoki/pkcsslotd.socket
      Owner: PKCSSLOTD_USER  Group: PKCS_GROUP  Mode: 0660 (rw-rw----)

   b. Unix socket between pkcsslotd and event sources (e.g. pkcshsm_mk_change)
      to deliver events to tokens of running openCryptoki applications.
      Path: /run/opencryptoki/pkcsslotd.admin.socket
      Owner: PKCSSLOTD_USER  Group: PKCS_GROUP  Mode: 0660 (rw-rw----)

   c. Netlink socket owned by pkcsslotd to listen for udev events (s390 platform
      only). This is used to produce events on APQNs becoming online or offline.

   Note: pkcsslotd also uses an epoll file descriptor internally to multiplex
   all of the above, but it is not a socket and leaves no on-disk resource.

3. Files
    Note: on Linux the runtime directory is /run. On AIX it is /var/run.
    All paths below that start with /run/opencryptoki/ are therefore
    /var/run/opencryptoki/ on AIX.

    a. Directories
       The following directories are created by pkcsslotd at startup if they
       do not already exist. They are normally pre-created by tmpfiles.d.

       /run/opencryptoki/
           Owner: PKCSSLOTD_USER  Group: PKCS_GROUP  Mode: 0710 (rwx--x---)
       /var/lock/opencryptoki/
           Owner: PKCSSLOTD_USER  Group: PKCS_GROUP  Mode: 0770 (rwxrwx---)
       /var/log/opencryptoki/
           Owner: PKCSSLOTD_USER  Group: PKCS_GROUP  Mode: 0770 (rwxrwx---)
       /var/lib/opencryptoki/
           Owner: PKCSSLOTD_USER  Group: PKCS_GROUP  Mode: 0770 (rwxrwx---)
       /var/lib/opencryptoki/HSM_MK_CHANGE/
           Owner: PKCSSLOTD_USER  Group: PKCS_GROUP  Mode: 0770 (rwxrwx---)

       Each token's data directory (e.g. /var/lib/opencryptoki/swtok/) and its
       TOK_OBJ/ subdirectory are created by pkcsslotd when a token is first
       seen, or by the 'pkcstok_admin create' command.
       When created by pkcsslotd (only possible when TOKEN_GROUP == PKCS_GROUP;
       if usergroup= is set to a different group, pkcsslotd refuses and requires
       'pkcstok_admin create' to be used instead):
           Owner: PKCSSLOTD_USER  Group: TOKEN_GROUP  Mode: 0770 (rwxrwx---)
       When created by 'pkcstok_admin create' (must be run as root):
           Owner: root  Group: TOKEN_GROUP  Mode: 0770 (rwxrwx---)
       Use 'pkcstok_admin chown' to reassign group ownership after creation.

       The TPM token uses per-user subdirectories instead:
           /var/lib/opencryptoki/tpm/${USER}/
           Owner: the user  Group: the user's primary group  Mode: 0700

    b. Lock files
       All lock files are owned by whoever creates the file first.
       LCK..APIlock is created by pkcsslotd (owner: PKCSSLOTD_USER).
       LCK..HSM_MK_CHANGElock is created by pkcshsm_mk_change or the first
       application to acquire it (owner: that process's user).
       Per-token lock subdirectories and lock files are created by the
       application process and are thus owned by the application user.
       Mode: 0440 (r--r-----) Linux / 0220 (-w--w----) AIX
       # ls /var/lock/opencryptoki/
       LCK..APIlock              (Owner: PKCSSLOTD_USER  Group: PKCS_GROUP)
       LCK..HSM_MK_CHANGElock    (Owner: application user  Group: PKCS_GROUP)
       ccatok/LCK..ccatok        (Owner: application user  Group: TOKEN_GROUP)
       ep11tok/LCK..ep11tok      (Owner: application user  Group: TOKEN_GROUP)
       icsf/LCK..icsf            (Owner: application user  Group: TOKEN_GROUP)
       lite/LCK..lite            (Owner: application user  Group: TOKEN_GROUP)
       swtok/LCK..swtok          (Owner: application user  Group: TOKEN_GROUP)
       tpm/<USER>/LCK..tpm       (Owner: application user  Group: TOKEN_GROUP)

    c. Trace files
       Generated per process when OPENCRYPTOKI_TRACE_LEVEL is set.
       Path: /var/log/opencryptoki/trace.<pid>
       Owner: the process owner  Group: PKCS_GROUP  Mode: 0640 (rw-r-----)
       No size limit; one file per process while tracing is active.

    d. Config files (some are optional)
       # ls /etc/opencryptoki/
       opencryptoki.conf          root:root       0644  main slot configuration
       ep11tok.conf               root:root       0644  EP11 token configuration
                                                        (name set via confname= in opencryptoki.conf)
       ep11cpfilter.conf          root:root       0644  EP11 CP-filter config
                                                        (name set via CPFILTER in ep11tok.conf)
       ccatok.conf                root:root       0644  CCA token configuration
                                                        (name set via confname= in opencryptoki.conf)
       <tokenname>.conf           root:root       0644  ICSF token configuration
                                                        (created by pkcsicsf, name = ICSF token name)
       p11kmip.conf               root:PKCS_GROUP 0640  p11kmip tool config
       p11sak_defined_attrs.conf  root:PKCS_GROUP 0640  p11sak custom attributes
       policy.conf                root:PKCS_GROUP 0640  key policy configuration
       strength.conf              root:PKCS_GROUP 0640  key strength configuration

    e. PID file - created by pkcsslotd at startup
       Path: /run/opencryptoki/pkcsslotd.pid
       Owner: PKCSSLOTD_USER  Group: PKCS_GROUP  Mode: 0644 (rw-r--r--)
       Size: a few bytes (ASCII decimal PID followed by newline).
       Note: pkcsslotd drops root privileges via setuid/setgid + execv before
       any files are created, so all files it writes are owned by
       PKCSSLOTD_USER with primary group PKCS_GROUP.

    f. Token data files
       3 files per token + 1 additional RACF file for the ICSF token
       + wrapped key files for the TPM token (per user).
       Owner: the application user performing the operation (C_InitToken,
              C_SetPIN, etc.)  Group: TOKEN_GROUP  Mode: 0660 (rw-rw----)
       (TPM token: owner = the user, no group sharing, mode 0600)

       NVTOK.DAT  - Token metadata (label, flags, PIN hashes, version info).
                    Size: sizeof(TOKEN_DATA), a fixed ~400-byte structure.
       MK_SO      - Master key encrypted with the SO PIN. Not present on TPM
                    token.
       MK_USER    - Master key encrypted with the USER PIN. Not present on TPM
                    token.
       RACF       - ICSF token only: encrypted RACF password.
       /var/lib/opencryptoki/tpm/${USER}/PRIVATE_ROOT_KEY.pem
       /var/lib/opencryptoki/tpm/${USER}/PUBLIC_ROOT_KEY.pem
                  - TPM token only: per-user software root key pair.

    g. Token object files
       One OBJ.IDX index file and one binary file per stored token object,
       all inside the token's TOK_OBJ/ directory.
       Both file types are written by the application process and share the
       same ownership model: the owner is the application user that performed
       the operation (who must be a member of TOKEN_GROUP).
       Group: TOKEN_GROUP  Mode: 0660 (rw-rw----)
       (TPM token: mode 0600, no group access)
       OBJ.IDX   - Text index listing the names of all current token objects,
                   one per line. Appended to when objects are created,
                   rewritten (via IDX.TMP) when objects are deleted.
       OBxxxxxx  - Individual token object files. Each file stores one
                   serialized PKCS#11 object in binary format (encrypted for
                   private objects). The 8-character filename is generated by
                   mkstemp() using the template "OBXXXXXX" and is never reused.
       The maximum number of token objects per token is MAX_TOK_OBJS
       (default: 2048 public + 2048 private). Configurable at build time:
           ./configure --with-max-token-objects=N

    h. HSM master key change state files
       /var/lib/opencryptoki/HSM_MK_CHANGE/
           Directory created by pkcsslotd; used by pkcshsm_mk_change to
           persist MK change operation state across slots.
       State files within that directory are written by pkcshsm_mk_change:
           Owner: the user running pkcshsm_mk_change  Group: PKCS_GROUP
           Mode: 0660 (rw-rw----)
